AU  - MacKenzie, I. Scott
AU  - Staab, Steffen
PY  - 2020
AB  - We present the design and evaluation of Talk-and-Gaze (TaG), a method for selecting and correcting errors with voice and gaze. TaG uses eye gaze to overcome the inability of voice-only systems to provide spatial information. The user's point of gaze is used to select an erroneous word either by dwelling on the word for 800 ms (D-TaG) or by uttering a "select" voice command (V-TaG). A user study with 12 participants compared D-TaG, V-TaG, and a voice-only method for selecting and correcting words. Corrections were performed more than 20\% faster with D-TaG compared to the V-TaG or voice-only methods. As well, D-TaG was observed to require 24\% less selection effort than V-TaG and 11\% less selection effort than voice-only error correction. D-TaG was well received in a subjective assessment with 66\% of users choosing it as their preferred choice for error correction in voice-based text entry.
